WEBVTT

00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:07.269
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Monday the second of March. Can you hear me over that fan?</v>

00:00:08.990 --> 00:00:14.589
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, you sound like you're calling from inside a tumble dryer, but we can hear you.</v>

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:18.359
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely. Professional start, then.</v>

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:26.460
<v Jamie Brennan>Before we start, whose new car's that in the car park? The blue one taking up most of the county.</v>

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:32.799
<v Callum Reid>Not mine. Mine's the one worth less than the tyres on it.</v>

00:00:34.109 --> 00:00:36.210
<v David Whitfield>That doesn't narrow it down much.</v>

00:00:38.229 --> 00:00:41.380
<v Jamie Brennan>Honestly, you need a banksman to get past it.</v>

00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:45.789
<v Hannah Price>It's parked inside the lines, to be fair.</v>

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:49.469
<v Jamie Brennan>Only just. Anyway, very nice. Not jealous at all.</v>

00:00:50.469 --> 00:00:51.869
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, motoring section finished?</v>

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:56.070
<v Priya Raman>Please. Some of us haven't even had a coffee.</v>

00:00:57.850 --> 00:01:03.799
<v Sarah Okafor>Tomasz Nowak isn't with us today. Everyone else is on, so let's get through the updates first.</v>

00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:09.370
<v Callum Reid>I'm here, just on the headset. Bit noisy this end.</v>

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:13.420
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, you're dipping in and out a bit.</v>

00:01:14.469 --> 00:01:16.569
<v Callum Reid>Typical. Worked perfectly before I joined.</v>

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:26.099
<v Priya Raman>Callum asked me to pass on his near-miss write-up update: he's been working through it, still on it, and it's going fine so far.</v>

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:31.760
<v Sarah Okafor>Cheers. I can hear you much better than him, anyway.</v>

00:01:32.909 --> 00:01:35.010
<v Callum Reid>I heard that bit, funnily enough.</v>

00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:37.829
<v David Whitfield>Selective headset. We've all had one.</v>

00:01:39.890 --> 00:01:42.340
<v Sarah Okafor>Go on, then, what have you got?</v>

00:01:44.150 --> 00:01:50.099
<v David Whitfield>Cal also gave me a message about the other near-miss write-up. He's about halfway through that one.</v>

00:01:52.079 --> 00:01:53.280
<v Callum Reid>Cheers, mate.</v>

00:01:55.530 --> 00:01:56.730
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. Quality?</v>

00:01:57.930 --> 00:01:59.680
<v Hannah Price>Yep, two bits from me.</v>

00:02:01.480 --> 00:02:07.079
<v Hannah Price>That jam clearance and sensor check from before, the one nobody had taken—I'll take that on.</v>

00:02:09.009 --> 00:02:11.110
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Pricey. That's with you, then.</v>

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:15.219
<v Hannah Price>And, um, the less cheerful bit.</v>

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:24.120
<v Hannah Price>I can't get any further with inspecting the relief valve for leaks. I need an electrician to isolate it first.</v>

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:25.949
<v Priya Raman>Right, understood.</v>

00:02:26.539 --> 00:02:29.689
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, thanks for flagging it. What about you, Haley?</v>

00:02:31.169 --> 00:02:33.620
<v Marcus Hale>Sorry, was muted. Talking away to myself.</v>

00:02:34.270 --> 00:02:37.069
<v Marcus Hale>The guarding check's all done. Boxed that off.</v>

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:39.439
<v Sarah Okafor>Good, cheers.</v>

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:43.199
<v Marcus Hale>That's me, really. Short and sweet for once.</v>

00:02:45.639 --> 00:02:51.939
<v Sarah Okafor>Mine's quick as well: the pressure-drop investigation on the power pack on one is finished, all signed off.</v>

00:02:54.389 --> 00:02:58.590
<v David Whitfield>Nice. Always good to get a signature at the end of it.</v>

00:02:59.139 --> 00:03:02.639
<v Sarah Okafor>You had something else, didn't you? Sorry, nearly skipped you.</v>

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:09.770
<v David Whitfield>Just a bit of history—the inspection on the long belt, I signed that off on Tuesday. That's already done.</v>

00:03:11.449 --> 00:03:12.650
<v Sarah Okafor>Ah, yes. Thanks.</v>

00:03:14.310 --> 00:03:16.409
<v David Whitfield>Tuesday feels about a month ago.</v>

00:03:18.379 --> 00:03:20.479
<v Callum Reid>Yeah. Right, on the new stuff—</v>

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:25.090
<v Callum Reid>I'll do the pre-use checks on the trucks next week.</v>

00:03:26.270 --> 00:03:29.770
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Cal. Not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:32.909
<v Callum Reid>Yep, next week. I've got it.</v>

00:03:33.990 --> 00:03:37.139
<v Marcus Hale>Sorry, I spoke over the end there. Teams lag.</v>

00:03:38.669 --> 00:03:41.469
<v Callum Reid>No worries. Think everyone got the important bit.</v>

00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:44.599
<v Sarah Okafor>They did. Anything new from stores Jamie?</v>

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:52.629
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah so, I'll recalibrate the sensors on the boiler safety valve this afternoon. That's fairly important.</v>

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:55.819
<v Sarah Okafor>Agreed, stores Jamie. This afternoon for that.</v>

00:03:58.199 --> 00:03:59.599
<v Jamie Brennan>Yep, I'll do it.</v>

00:04:00.330 --> 00:04:05.580
<v Priya Raman>Heard you. You went a bit robotic at the start, but the rest came through.</v>

00:04:05.949 --> 00:04:07.699
<v Jamie Brennan>That's just my Monday voice.</v>

00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:12.250
<v Hannah Price>Remarkably similar to your Friday voice.</v>

00:04:12.830 --> 00:04:16.680
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, unless anyone's being cut off, that's everything for this morning.</v>

00:04:17.399 --> 00:04:18.600
<v Marcus Hale>All heard here.</v>

00:04:20.189 --> 00:04:21.589
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely. Thanks, everyone. Cheers.</v>
